  "title": "Can More Vitamin D During Pregnancy Make Children Smarter?",
  "summary": "Vitamin D is an important nutrient during pregnancy, supporting normal bone development and overall health. But could taking more vitamin D while pregnant also influence a child’s brain development years later? A new study from Denmark has raised that possibility. Researchers found that children whose mothers received a higher dose of vitamin D during the later stages of pregnancy performed slightly better on certain memory tests when they were around ten years old. The results are interesting",
